@HostAddress = http://localhost:8080
# Admin requests read the key from an environment variable so it never lands in this file:
#   export DOTADRAFT_ADMIN_KEY="$(dotnet user-secrets list --project DotaDraft.Api | sed -n 's/^Admin:ApiKey = //p')"
@AdminKey = {{$processEnv DOTADRAFT_ADMIN_KEY}}

### List heroes
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/heroes
Accept: application/json

### Top counter-picks for a hero (here Anti-Mage), ranked by sample-adjusted advantage; limit is 1-20
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/heroes/1/counters?limit=5
Accept: application/json

### Seed heroes from OpenDota (run before seeding matchups)
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/admin/seed-heroes
X-Admin-Key: {{AdminKey}}

### Queue matchup seeding as a background job (returns 202; takes a few minutes)
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/admin/seed-matchups
X-Admin-Key: {{AdminKey}}

### Matchup seeding job status
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/admin/seed-matchups/status
X-Admin-Key: {{AdminKey}}
Accept: application/json

### Health: "Healthy" (200) when the database is reachable, "Unhealthy" (503) otherwise
GET {{HostAddress}}/health
